WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:02.940
<b>Tuldarr    Treasury</b>

00:07.780 --> 00:09.570
This place is a treasure trove!

00:09.570 --> 00:11.580
Well, it <i>is</i> the treasury.

00:11.990 --> 00:15.160
Let's decide what we're 
going to take back to Farsas.

00:15.600 --> 00:17.770
I'll bring any dubious items back to my tower,

00:17.770 --> 00:19.810
so please separate those as well.

00:19.810 --> 00:21.070
Yes!

00:19.810 --> 00:21.070
I'll do my best.

00:32.060 --> 00:33.040
Huh?

00:33.040 --> 00:34.740
Where have I seen this before?

00:36.270 --> 00:38.510
I'll bring it back to the tower for now.

02:10.230 --> 02:14.980
~ Green Vines ~

02:14.980 --> 02:17.400
<b>Minnedart Fortress    Eastern Farsas, Bordering Yarda</b>

02:17.950 --> 02:20.660
Are things the same around the eastern border?

02:20.660 --> 02:23.620
<b>Edgard    Farsas General</b>

02:21.030 --> 02:23.860
No signs of unusual movements 
from neighboring nations,

02:23.860 --> 02:25.910
although there are minor conflicts.

02:30.580 --> 02:33.540
<b>Galen    Farsas General</b>

02:31.900 --> 02:36.310
A nearby village was attacked 
by horse riders a year ago.

02:36.770 --> 02:41.010
We sent out soldiers as fast as we could, 
but most of the townsmen were killed,

02:41.540 --> 02:44.220
so we brought the survivors here.

02:44.720 --> 02:46.600
Horse riders...

02:46.600 --> 02:47.700
You mean the Ito?

02:47.700 --> 02:48.720
Yes.

02:48.720 --> 02:52.980
Nomads who swiftly rush in 
to plunder all they can.

02:52.980 --> 02:54.130
Elze!

02:54.130 --> 02:55.690
Elze!

02:55.690 --> 02:58.290
That's Elze, the village chief's widow.

02:58.290 --> 03:03.670
He died protecting her, 
and she hasn't laughed since.

03:04.210 --> 03:05.620
Poor girl.

03:07.130 --> 03:10.690
Nowadays, she spends 
all her time playing with the children.

03:12.870 --> 03:17.300
Once upon a time, when our village 
was in the grasslands,

03:17.770 --> 03:20.630
there lived a very 
beautiful girl in the village.

03:21.530 --> 03:27.830
She had countless young suitors, but she 
would not take one as her husband.

03:27.830 --> 03:29.820
I bet there were no good men there!

03:29.820 --> 03:30.850
Shh.

03:31.900 --> 03:36.010
One day, the village was attacked 
by evil men on horseback.

03:36.970 --> 03:42.030
They set fire to the houses, burning 
the village down to try and kill its people.

03:42.380 --> 03:46.380
But then there appeared 
a swordsman clad in blue.

03:47.450 --> 03:53.040
He chased the evil men away 
and saved the girl from being abducted.

03:53.490 --> 03:57.750
Deeply moved, she asked 
to take his hand in marriage,

03:58.260 --> 04:02.870
but he turned her down 
and left without a trace.

04:04.910 --> 04:05.830
The end.

04:07.350 --> 04:09.090
The swordsman's so awesome!

04:09.090 --> 04:11.580
Hey! Let's have a pretend fight over there!

04:11.580 --> 04:12.600
Yeah!

04:12.600 --> 04:13.860
Me too!

04:17.230 --> 04:18.320
My apologies.

04:18.650 --> 04:21.270
I was curious about the story you told them.

04:22.670 --> 04:28.740
This story is actually based on a true tale 
of two hundred years ago from our village.

04:29.540 --> 04:34.330
The blue swordsman claimed to be 
the son of the girl he saved.

04:34.930 --> 04:36.020
Um...

04:36.020 --> 04:39.710
You mean he had come from the future?

04:40.620 --> 04:42.430
Yes, that's right.

04:42.430 --> 04:48.300
The blue swordsman was the child of the girl 
and a nomad who abducted her back then.

04:48.730 --> 04:53.380
He said he traveled to the past 
to change his mother's misfortune.

04:54.640 --> 04:59.340
If he changed his past, 
he would cease to be born.

04:59.340 --> 05:03.180
But knowing this, he still saved his mother.

05:03.180 --> 05:04.660
That's how the story goes.

05:05.530 --> 05:07.190
What would you have done?

05:09.190 --> 05:10.780
If it was me...

05:13.050 --> 05:14.890
I wouldn't change the past.

05:19.010 --> 05:20.460
You've outdone yourself.

05:21.010 --> 05:24.780
I wasn't sure what we'd do when I heard 
they only had one room available,

05:25.460 --> 05:28.180
but I didn't think you'd 
turn yourself into a cat.

05:28.520 --> 05:32.510
<i>Sharing a room is perfect, 
since I can tell if you sneak out at night.</i>

05:32.510 --> 05:34.480
You really don't trust me, huh?

05:34.770 --> 05:37.490
<i>I don't know why you think I would.</i>

05:41.150 --> 05:43.410
Are you going to spend 
all of tomorrow like this?

06:07.050 --> 06:07.970
What's wrong?

06:08.950 --> 06:10.930
<i>I synced with them!</i>

06:10.930 --> 06:12.290
Synced?

06:12.290 --> 06:13.890
Calm down and explain yourself.

06:15.110 --> 06:20.400
<i>I fell into a deep sleep and tuned 
into a matching dream frequency.</i>

06:20.400 --> 06:22.010
What does that mean?

06:22.010 --> 06:27.740
<i>In this fortress, someone is broadcasting 
a dream with strong emotions while asleep.</i>

06:28.210 --> 06:33.330
<i>It's most likely someone with magical power, 
who never learned to control it.</i>

06:33.330 --> 06:34.830
What kind of dream was it?

06:35.950 --> 06:38.960
<i>A dream of someone they hate and can't forget.</i>

06:43.430 --> 06:47.550
I hear our neighbor Yarda has been 
turning into desert more and more lately.

06:47.550 --> 06:48.680
Yes.

06:48.680 --> 06:51.260
For now, there haven't been 
any conspicuous movements,

06:51.260 --> 06:53.240
but we'll continue to keep an eye out.

06:53.240 --> 06:53.960
Please do.

06:55.070 --> 06:56.600
We should get back.

06:56.600 --> 06:58.610
We still need to visit all the villages.

07:09.280 --> 07:10.370
The Ito, huh?

07:11.400 --> 07:12.730
Stay still, Tinasha.

07:12.730 --> 07:13.820
Be a good girl.

07:18.300 --> 07:19.740
My name is Javi.

07:20.460 --> 07:21.990
I'm the leader of the Ito.

07:22.740 --> 07:24.670
There's something you have that we want.

07:25.050 --> 07:27.350
Pretty demanding for a thief.

07:27.350 --> 07:30.380
I have no qualms about taking all of you out.

07:30.380 --> 07:33.100
It's clear that your threats are empty.

07:33.100 --> 07:37.350
Say what you will, but plundering
 is our clan's way of life.

07:37.350 --> 07:39.560
The strong take for themselves.

07:39.950 --> 07:42.620
We take pride in our way of living!

07:45.590 --> 07:46.860
What do you want?

07:47.810 --> 07:48.860
A woman.

07:49.220 --> 07:50.060
A woman?

07:50.470 --> 07:54.450
The woman I failed to kidnap a year ago.

07:54.450 --> 07:55.700
With her as the prize...

07:56.110 --> 07:58.290
we'll have a duel on the red rock plateau!

08:01.670 --> 08:03.710
It's like a cage for a giant.

08:03.710 --> 08:05.670
This land is sacred to the Ito.

08:06.370 --> 08:10.200
It's said that a god visited 
this place long ago.

08:10.200 --> 08:11.040
A god?

08:11.040 --> 08:13.690
Aetea? Or one of Aetea's children?

08:14.130 --> 08:15.820
Neither.

08:15.820 --> 08:17.870
The name has been lost.

08:18.350 --> 08:19.850
A god from another land.

08:20.140 --> 08:21.410
Another land?

08:22.200 --> 08:24.750
<i>I sense something strange with this place.</i>

08:25.520 --> 08:29.960
<i>I can teleport everyone, 
so why don't we do this somewhere else?</i>

08:29.960 --> 08:32.120
<i>Like the castle training grounds?</i>

08:32.120 --> 08:35.620
That sounds interesting, 
but our opponents won't oblige.

08:35.620 --> 08:37.420
We just need to hurry up and win.

08:38.740 --> 08:43.580
If I win this duel, I forbid you 
from ever looting on Farsas land.

08:44.030 --> 08:47.690
You can imagine what awaits you if you do.

08:56.930 --> 08:58.640
Have you heard the details?

08:59.280 --> 09:04.850
Th-That man killed my husband.

09:06.740 --> 09:09.820
He must be someone you hate.

09:10.220 --> 09:12.530
I-I...

09:13.750 --> 09:14.990
It's been a while.

09:18.460 --> 09:19.990
I'm here for you.

09:32.050 --> 09:33.210
Begin!

09:58.390 --> 10:00.080
This duel's over.

10:00.080 --> 10:01.750
Time to keep your promise.

10:06.450 --> 10:08.490
Elze...

10:26.950 --> 10:28.980
<i>So it was her dream.</i>

10:33.410 --> 10:36.460
Tinasha, can you reattach his arm?

10:36.460 --> 10:38.140
<i>No thanks.</i>

10:38.140 --> 10:39.860
Then at least stop his bleeding.

10:48.300 --> 10:50.010
<i>That should do it.</i>

11:00.630 --> 11:02.170
Get away from there!

11:09.060 --> 11:10.570
What's going on?

11:10.570 --> 11:12.520
<i>I'll teleport them.</i>

11:15.070 --> 11:16.410
This isn't good.

11:16.410 --> 11:18.500
<i>We need to stop that thing.</i>

11:18.500 --> 11:19.440
Yeah.

11:21.330 --> 11:22.160
Tinasha?

11:28.140 --> 11:28.790
That's...

11:45.220 --> 11:46.140
Tinasha!

12:07.070 --> 12:08.930
Are you okay, Tinasha?

12:10.030 --> 12:10.830
<i>No...</i>

12:11.580 --> 12:12.420
No?

12:12.870 --> 12:14.340
<i>No, no, no!</i>

12:14.340 --> 12:16.330
<i>I hate being wet as a cat!</i>

12:15.290 --> 12:16.330
What's wrong?

12:16.330 --> 12:17.820
Calm down a little!

12:17.820 --> 12:19.610
Just turn back into a human!

12:24.420 --> 12:26.480
What exactly <i>is</i> this place?

12:26.480 --> 12:28.350
I'd like to know as well.

12:30.350 --> 12:31.740
Are you okay?

12:31.740 --> 12:34.220
You looked like you weren't 
feeling well earlier.

12:34.220 --> 12:37.170
That was because of 
outside magical interference.

12:37.170 --> 12:41.220
Some sort of power from the earth 
attacked the magic in my body.

12:41.890 --> 12:44.170
It felt like it was digging through my insides.

12:44.170 --> 12:46.740
I was too creeped out to form any spells.

12:45.410 --> 12:47.120
<b>Ito Sacred Grounds</b>

12:50.030 --> 12:52.790
We're directly under the Ito sacred grounds.

12:53.180 --> 12:56.580
Is this their history carved into the walls?

12:57.000 --> 12:58.110
"Past"...

12:58.610 --> 12:59.930
"Magic spheres"...

13:01.290 --> 13:02.980
"Memories of a clan"?

13:04.270 --> 13:05.220
Oscar.

13:06.540 --> 13:11.170
This must be the visiting god 
that attacked us earlier.

13:11.890 --> 13:17.410
"The deity from the north found the devil 
fiends hiding among humans and killed them."

13:17.410 --> 13:20.840
"All gave thanks to the deity, 
but with fear in their hearts."

13:20.840 --> 13:23.290
"They made a place for it to rest," it says.

13:24.280 --> 13:29.660
"Devil fiend" is a pejorative term for 
mages used in the early Dark Age.

13:30.150 --> 13:33.830
At the time, mages weren't treated as humans.

13:34.380 --> 13:38.280
This god reacted to magic 
and revealed any mages,

13:38.280 --> 13:40.620
so the Ito must have found it useful.

13:41.330 --> 13:43.530
So they made their 
sacred land its resting place?

13:43.950 --> 13:48.360
But what could it really be, 
if it reacts to magic?

13:48.360 --> 13:50.460
It looked like mist, but is it a demon?

13:50.830 --> 13:52.260
No, it's not.

13:52.610 --> 13:54.270
That's not what this is.

13:56.130 --> 13:57.940
Rity...di...?

13:58.810 --> 14:04.300
Before it, those with magic find themselves 
affected physically and mentally.

14:04.300 --> 14:07.050
Their magic runs wild 
and harms those around them.

14:07.050 --> 14:08.050
You don't mean...

14:10.870 --> 14:13.910
The deity worshiped by the powerful 
nation to the north of the mainland:

14:14.930 --> 14:18.460
Irityrdia, the one true god of Tayiri?

14:19.620 --> 14:22.050
The one responsible 
for the persecution of mages...

14:24.180 --> 14:26.640
Oscar, could you wait here—

14:26.640 --> 14:27.160
No thanks.

14:27.160 --> 14:28.180
Of course!

14:28.180 --> 14:30.130
I figured that was the case.

14:30.130 --> 14:32.270
I want to teleport you back home 
against your will!

14:32.600 --> 14:34.960
Wait, are you going to be okay?

14:34.960 --> 14:36.850
Aren't you going to react like you did earlier?

14:36.850 --> 14:39.130
I'll put up a defensive wall.

14:39.130 --> 14:40.790
I'm not a cat this time, either.

14:41.220 --> 14:45.810
You don't have Akashia, 
which is why I'm worried about you.

14:47.500 --> 14:49.340
I'll borrow this, since it's right here.

15:00.250 --> 15:01.170
Stay away.

15:02.920 --> 15:04.930
If you reach your limit, you can turn back.

15:13.770 --> 15:14.710
Elze.

15:23.560 --> 15:25.690
She's been possessed by Irityrdia?

15:26.050 --> 15:27.170
That's not good.

15:31.610 --> 15:33.450
Hey, <i>that's</i> your move?

15:42.350 --> 15:43.580
Not bad.

15:44.290 --> 15:45.340
Are you okay?

15:45.340 --> 15:46.810
Your face is pale.

15:46.810 --> 15:49.130
It feels like I'm really seasick.

15:49.450 --> 15:51.340
I don't feel anything like that.

15:51.690 --> 15:57.390
Half of my magic was acquired after birth, 
so I'm more easily affected.

15:58.020 --> 16:01.460
Whereas your magic has been sealed away.

16:01.460 --> 16:02.550
Sealed away?

16:03.020 --> 16:06.460
I'd love to hear about that, 
so I'll ask you later.

16:06.980 --> 16:07.730
So?

16:08.330 --> 16:12.700
Can we do something about 
Irityrdia here without killing Elze?

16:13.390 --> 16:15.000
It won't be easy.

16:15.000 --> 16:17.880
It's strong against magic, 
so we can't drag it out.

16:17.880 --> 16:22.100
That said, it's impossible to destroy 
what's inside without damaging her body.

16:22.100 --> 16:27.610
Perhaps that human figure carved on 
the wall was a possessed human as well.

16:28.170 --> 16:30.330
First, we need Akashia.

16:31.070 --> 16:34.210
It seems it has the power 
to annihilate even Irityrdia.

16:35.810 --> 16:36.820
Oscar.

16:37.260 --> 16:37.950
Yeah.

16:38.300 --> 16:42.370
But if I slice through Elze with Akashia, 
she's good as dead.

16:42.370 --> 16:43.000
Yes.

16:43.000 --> 16:46.020
That said, if this being escapes from here...

16:50.090 --> 16:52.900
I can't let you kill her.

16:53.860 --> 16:55.610
I understand how you feel,

16:56.000 --> 17:00.580
but it would be catastrophic to let her 
outside while possessed by Irityrdia.

17:01.460 --> 17:06.040
Just by going near her, those with magic 
will end up dead or insane.

17:06.520 --> 17:10.000
If a mage goes berserk, the people 
around them will be in danger, too.

17:10.590 --> 17:13.970
That thing is a phenomenon 
that propagates innocent deaths.

17:14.290 --> 17:17.340
Do you want to repeat the mistakes of history?

17:17.980 --> 17:19.930
If you can't even understand that much...

17:20.330 --> 17:22.770
we can start by killing you first.

17:25.500 --> 17:30.550
I don't care who she kills, or how many people.

17:32.290 --> 17:35.070
Please save her.

17:38.290 --> 17:39.970
If you insist.

17:43.820 --> 17:47.910
If I become a threat to the world...

17:48.550 --> 17:50.140
would you please kill me?

17:54.620 --> 17:58.930
Only if there was no way to change that fact.

18:07.450 --> 18:11.300
I can keep fighting, 
because that's how you are.

18:16.770 --> 18:17.730
Let's get started.

18:25.310 --> 18:26.620
Irityrdia.

18:27.020 --> 18:29.580
I know I'm the one who has awakened you.

18:29.580 --> 18:32.380
You were within an ancient seal,

18:32.380 --> 18:37.060
but you reacted to my magic 
and awoke, possessing that girl.

18:37.770 --> 18:39.010
Face me.

18:39.010 --> 18:44.270
O god who has killed and driven mad 
so many, and left a blemish on history.

18:44.270 --> 18:47.010
As a mage of this mainland...

18:47.680 --> 18:50.020
I, the Witch of the Azure Moon, 
will be your foe.

18:53.260 --> 18:54.190
Don't leave me!

19:03.410 --> 19:04.160
Come.

19:05.830 --> 19:07.310
Tinasha! Stop!

19:11.750 --> 19:12.950
Tinasha!

19:14.590 --> 19:16.670
Not yet.

19:16.930 --> 19:18.420
What do you mean, not yet?

19:18.420 --> 19:20.380
I'll make you spit out that crystal ball.

19:20.380 --> 19:23.690
But then it might get away.

19:26.130 --> 19:27.370
It's here.

19:27.370 --> 19:28.690
You've got this, right?

19:29.350 --> 19:30.730
I swear...

19:30.730 --> 19:33.560
You want me to slice your stomach open?

19:33.920 --> 19:37.220
I know you can do the job 
with the smallest possible wound.

19:37.220 --> 19:39.120
You're really asking the impossible here.

19:39.120 --> 19:41.530
Could it be that you 
don't have any confidence?

19:41.530 --> 19:42.900
Don't egg me on, idiot!

19:42.900 --> 19:44.990
I'm just sick of you always using me.

19:45.300 --> 19:46.360
Are you a cat?

19:46.360 --> 19:47.860
No, I'm not.

19:53.150 --> 19:55.490
Fine, I'll do it.

20:01.750 --> 20:04.760
You're the one and only one for me.

20:08.070 --> 20:09.560
I'll beat it without a sweat.

20:09.560 --> 20:11.580
Yes, of course.

20:13.110 --> 20:14.290
Oscar.

20:14.290 --> 20:19.580
For so, <i>so</i> long, I've wanted 
to give this god a good beating.

20:20.970 --> 20:23.390
So please.

20:38.590 --> 20:39.750
Are you okay?

20:40.220 --> 20:42.920
There aren't any shards left inside, are there?

20:42.920 --> 20:45.950
I'd be able to tell if there were.

20:45.950 --> 20:47.060
I'm fine.

20:47.940 --> 20:49.640
What about the girl?

20:49.960 --> 20:53.350
Elze received treatment 
and was left in the village ruins.

20:53.640 --> 20:56.560
If she feels like it, 
she'll come back on her own.

20:57.190 --> 20:58.370
I suppose.

21:03.740 --> 21:06.140
You're going to sleep in your human form?

21:06.140 --> 21:08.450
Have you forgotten we're sharing a room?

21:08.450 --> 21:11.780
I know that you have very strong self-control.

21:11.780 --> 21:13.840
That'll come back to bite you someday.

21:13.840 --> 21:16.620
I curl up into a ball when I'm a cat.

21:16.620 --> 21:18.270
I want to stretch my limbs.

21:19.820 --> 21:23.230
Let me sleep for just one hour.

21:23.880 --> 21:25.590
Get some proper rest.

21:32.380 --> 21:34.520
I'll protect you, no matter what.

21:48.980 --> 21:50.410
What was that?!

21:50.410 --> 21:51.570
Couldn't help myself.

21:51.990 --> 21:55.320
J-Just when I was about to fall asleep...

23:35.430 --> 23:39.980
~ The Things Unknown ~
